-- the setting layer, which the glycerol case demands and the table only gestures at. Every count so far
-- was taken under a list of operations chosen by hand, with the choice justified in a comment: these are
-- proper, that one is a reflection, that one no medium supplies. The justification belongs in the
-- construction. An operation is admitted by an observation when two things hold: the motion that performs
-- it runs faster than the observation resolves, and either it is a proper motion or the medium cannot
-- tell the molecule from its mirror image. Both are facts about the observation and the motion, not about
-- the molecule, so the group is a function of the pair and the count is a function of the triple.
--
-- a motion: the permutation it performs, the order of magnitude of its rate in inverse seconds, and
-- whether it is proper. A methyl rotation is proper and fast at any temperature anyone works at. A ring
-- flip is proper and its rate depends on the temperature. The exchange of two groups across a mirror
-- plane is not a motion in time at all -- nothing performs it -- and it is recorded as improper, which an
-- achiral medium supplies and a chiral one does not.
Motion : Type 0
Motion = (p : Nat → Nat) × ((r : Nat) × Bool)
